# Retentio Web Test Conventions

## Project Overview

Vite + React + TypeScript app for Retentio deck review, catalog, and auth. HTTP API via `src/lib/api.ts`. JWT in `localStorage` (`wordupx_token`). Local dev: `./utils/run-dev.sh` (see `docs/development.md`).

## Commit & PR Conventions

- Commit/PR title: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>` in imperative mood, under 50 chars
- Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore
- Scopes: auth, deck, card, fact, catalog, media, ui, api, ci
- Keep PRs focused; squash and merge for feature branches

## Code Style

- **TypeScript/React**: Vitest + Testing Library; Tailwind; React Router v6
- Prefer clear naming; comments only for non-obvious logic
- Stack patterns: `.cursor/react-web.mdc`, `.cursor/testing.mdc`

## Documentation

- User-facing docs: English + Chinese where the repo already pairs them (e.g. `docs/quickstart.md` + `docs/quickstart_zh.md`)
- Design docs: English only — see `design-docs.mdc`
- API contract: `../retentio-backend/docs/api.md`; update `docs/api_progress_tracker.md` when adding/changing API usage

## Key Principles

- Test failures: follow `validate-minimal-changes.mdc` (fix production code first)
- CI must pass before merge: `npm run test:run`, `npm run build` (see `ci-workflows.mdc`)

## Git & hooks

Feature branches only; never push to `main`. Hooks via `./utils/setup-hooks.sh` — see `git-workflow.mdc`.
